# Firebase / GCP compliance (Fireup project rule)

Hard project rule for all Fireup work (migrator and local data plane).

## No reverse-engineering

**Allowed:** public Google API docs; public protobuf/OpenAPI from `googleapis/googleapis`; documented emulator env vars (`FIRESTORE_EMULATOR_HOST`, etc.); open wire formats (gRPC, protobuf); Fireup first-party code.

**Forbidden:** decompile/disassemble/binary-analyze Google Firebase Emulator Suite, Cloud SDK closed components, or other proprietary Google/Firebase binaries; copy proprietary emulator source/assets that are not explicitly open-licensed; reconstruct undocumented closed behavior. If undocumented → defer or mark unsupported in the fidelity matrix.

SDK-compatible means speaking the **published** API surface for official clients — not cloning Google emulator internals.

## License recordkeeping

Keep `docs/licenses/FIREBASE_GCP_LOCAL.md` current on every PR that adds Google/Firebase-related code or protos (crate/path, version, SPDX, upstream URL/commit, use, attribution, decision).

Prefer Apache-2.0 / MIT public definitions. Generate stubs from public `.proto` via prost/tonic — do not vendor proprietary Java/Go emulator code. Do not strip copyright headers. Do not claim “official Firebase emulator” or Google affiliation.

## PR checklist

- [ ] No RE of proprietary binaries
- [ ] New deps/protos logged in the license ledger
- [ ] Undocumented behaviors deferred / listed unsupported
- [ ] Independent-implementation blurb preserved where relevant
